      "id": "0ps9rdh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Force"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Force is an external agent capable of changing the body's state of rest or motion.",
        "Newton's First Law defines inertia, Second Law provides force calculation (F = ma), and Third Law states action and reaction are equal and opposite.",
        "Work is calculated as the product of force and displacement in the direction of force (W = F × s × cos θ).",
        "Work done can be positive (θ < 90°), negative (θ > 90°), or zero (θ = 90° or zero displacement).",
        "Power represents the rate of doing work or energy consumption rate per unit time (P = W / t)."
      ],
      "id": "f78p2ct"
    },
